            <profile id="2661-b39a-144d-594b" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="af20-e256-4a51-93aa" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Hand weapons, buckler and javelins. Skirmishers. Any unit that chooses to flee or fire &amp; flee as a charge reaction rallies automatically at the end of its move and may reform facing in any direction; a charging enemy that encounters them does not destroy them and they may instead fight in the close combat phase (their opponents still count as charging). Dogs of War cannot be accompanied by characters and cannot benefit from the Army General and Standard Bearer rules. (Shieldwall p.79)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="f316-1298-9ffe-f2bc" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">6+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <!-- armour-save -->
            </profile>
          </profiles>
