  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="20f6-eedd-f945-acf4" name="Western Franks (Shieldwall) - List Notes" publicationId="af20-e256-4a51-93aa" hidden="false">
      <description>WESTERN FRANKS ARMY LISTS (Shieldwall, pp.66-76): Carolingian French, the County of Flanders, the Duchy of Normandy, the Bretons and Capetian French. Percentages are by points. Special rules p.72 (Ferocious Charge).
The Common/Uncommon pools differ between the compositions, so the units also belong to pool categories named after them. In the Carolingian French and Capetian lists the Common Warriors are the Milites alone.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Carolingian French]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Milites: at least 50%
  Uncommon Warriors: Pueri, Liberi, Coloni and Dogs of War: up to 33%
  Carolingian French (p.70). Characters up to 25%; Milites at least 50%; Pueri, Liberi, Coloni and Dogs of War (Vikings, Gestir, Stipendarii, Serjeants, Devroet) up to 33%. Milites may have bows (+1 pt); up to half of a unit of Milites, including mounted troops, may exchange shield and spear for bow (free), deployed in the rear ranks. Units of Liberi may be upgraded to Men of the Marches (+1 pt; Leadership 7). Every other unit of Pueri may exchange javelin and shield for bow.
[County of Flanders]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Common Warriors: Milites and Liberi: at least 50%
  Uncommon Warriors: Pueri, Coloni and Dogs of War: up to 25%
  The County of Flanders (pp.70-71). Characters up to 25%; Milites and Liberi at least 50%; Pueri, Coloni and Dogs of War (Vikings, Freebooters, Stipendarii, Serjeants) up to 25%. Dismounted Milites cost 15 pts each and have Shieldwall. Liberi cost 7 pts each and have Shieldwall; Liberi may be given light armour (+2 pts).
[Duchy of Normandy]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Common Warriors: Milites and Pueri: at least 50%
  Uncommon Warriors: Liberi, Coloni and Dogs of War: up to 33%
  The Duchy of Normandy (p.71). Characters up to 25%; a mounted Rex or Comes may have a lance (+4 pts). Milites and Pueri at least 50%; Liberi, Coloni and Dogs of War (Vikings, Stipendarii, Serjeants, Devroet) up to 33%. Mounted Milites cost 30 pts each and may exchange thrusting spear for lance (+4 pts); mounted Milites have Ferocious Charge.
[The Bretons]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Common Warriors: Milites and Pueri: at least 50%
  Uncommon Warriors: Coloni and Dogs of War: up to 25%
  The Bretons (p.71). Characters up to 25%; Milites and Pueri at least 50%; Coloni and Dogs of War (Vikings, Stipendarii, Serjeants) up to 25%. Mounted Milites cost 30 pts and have a BS of 4. Any character or unit of mounted Milites that chooses to flee or fire &amp; flee as a charge reaction rallies automatically at the end of its move and may reform facing in any direction; if the charging enemy encounters them they are not destroyed and may instead fight in the close combat phase (their opponents still count as charging). All mounted troops count as Light Cavalry. All Liberi may exchange their thrusting spears for throwing spears and count as Light Infantry.
[Capetian French]
  Characters: up to 33%
  Milites: at least 50%
  Uncommon Warriors: Pueri, Coloni and Dogs of War: up to 25%
  Capetian French (&amp; Late Carolingian French) (p.71). Characters up to 33%; Milites at least 50%; Pueri, Coloni and Dogs of War (Stipendarii, Serjeants, Cottereaux) up to 25%. Mounted Milites cost 29 pts each and have Ferocious Charge. At the beginning of each turn roll a dice for each character: on a 1 the character and any unit he is with must try to charge the closest enemy; if no enemy is within range they must move as far as possible directly towards the nearest enemy.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
